  "question": {
    "text": "Let f be a differentiable function on $\\mathbf{R}$ such that $\\mathrm{f}(2) = 1$, $f^{\\prime}(2)=4$. Let $\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0}(f(2+x))^{3 / x}=e^\\alpha$. Then the number of times the curve $y=4 x^3-4 x^2-4(\\alpha-7) x-\\alpha$ meets x -axis is :-",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wXn5L",
      "text": "$2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "K7KjA",
      "text": "$1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tKcnF",
      "text": "$0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EkLXn",
      "text": "$3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0}(f(2+x))^{\\frac{3}{x}} \\\\ & \\lim _{\\mathrm{e}^{x \\rightarrow 0}} \\frac{(f(2+x)-1) 3}{x} \\\\ & \\mathrm{e}^{3 f^{\\prime}(2)}=(e)^{12}=(e)^a \\Rightarrow a=12 \\\\ & y=4 x^3-4 x^2-4(a-7) x-a \\\\ & y=4 x^3-4 x^2-20 x-12 \\\\ & \\text { roots } x=-1,-1,3 \\\\ & \\text { option }(1)\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
